{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08V3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$t : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{B}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}'), \\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{B}'})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{J} = \\Ker(t^\\sharp)$", "MATH_0003": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{B})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{J} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0008": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-to-solve-ringed-topoi}\n\\vcenter{\n\\xymatrix{\n0 \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{G} \\ar[r] & {?} \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{O} \\ar[r] & 0 \\\\\n0 \\ar[r] & f^{-1}\\mathcal{J} \\ar[u]^c \\ar[r] &\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathcal{B}'} \\ar[u] \\ar[r] &\nf^{-1}\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{B} \\ar[u] \\ar[r] & 0\n}\n}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0009": "$i : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}')$", "MATH_0010": "$(f, f')$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Ker(i^\\sharp)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0013": "$(f')^\\sharp$", "MATH_0014": "$c$", "MATH_0015": "$(\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'), \\mathcal{O}')$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{defos-section-deformations-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{defos-equation-morphism-thickenings-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{equation-to-solve-ringed-topoi}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8738213de44f3dc51ec06708f87b0082057c6f2b1b4e6da5f14324b14d373dcc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a18c0eb310c3a43ef71fd4df561f7160c4a6a5c6ec66813d087b8c92d397bf83", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis section is the continuation of\nDeformation Theory, Section <REF_0001>\nwhich we urge the reader to read first. We briefly recall the setup.\nWe have a first order thickening\n<MATH_0001> of ringed topoi\nwith <MATH_0002>, a morphism of ringed topoi\n<MATH_0003>, an <MATH_0004>-module\n<MATH_0005>, and a map <MATH_0006>\nof sheaves of <MATH_0007>-modules.\nWe ask whether we can find\nthe question mark fitting into the following diagram\n<MATH_0008>\nand moreover how unique the solution is (if it exists). More precisely,\nwe look for a first order thickening\n<MATH_0009>\nand a morphism of thickenings <MATH_0010> as in\nDeformation Theory, Equation\n(<REF_0002>)\nwhere <MATH_0011> is identified with <MATH_0012>\nsuch that <MATH_0013> induces the given map <MATH_0014>.\nWe will say <MATH_0015> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>solution<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> to\n(<REF_0003>).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0ab2279a6ce85728c258d9bfb4ffd3360af3fbe7d541aca4f5055ecaf8832e1a", "unit_id": "tag:08V3:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08V3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\xi \\in \\Ext^2_\\mathcal{O}(L_f, \\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Ext^1_\\mathcal{O}(L_f, \\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0003": "$X'$", "MATH_0004": "$X'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Ext^0_\\mathcal{O}(L_f, \\mathcal{G})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-to-solve-ringed-topoi}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-to-solve-ringed-topoi}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-find-obstruction-ringed-topoi}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3ee78337b08d17bb82f072cadfa02e804ea5d7da40fe26c931883dd16665e36f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9fd6ea8e954bd34cd8ba4e05e9e58ba82faa6568064ceb991b38a40bf1c6fe04", "source_text": "In the situation above we have\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> There is a canonical element\n<MATH_0001>\nwhose vanishing is a sufficient and necessary condition for the existence\nof a solution to (<REF_0001>).\n<STRUCT_0003> If there exists a solution, then the set of\nisomorphism classes of solutions is principal homogeneous under\n<MATH_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Given a solution <MATH_0003>, the set of automorphisms of <MATH_0004>\nfitting into (<REF_0002>) is canonically isomorphic\nto <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a6cbe569b5ea97de8a109a0ea776f692fc5d5f56378698951f4ed34470cea06a", "unit_id": "tag:08V5:statement"}
